# MOVEMENT IV — file 74: b145-200 = RECAPITULATION.
# [K] b145-152 P ff tutti (vn1+fl at g5, vn2+ob 8vb) - now over the CELL
#     ostinato L4/L5 in vc/cb/fg instead of plain quarters; va tremolo.
# [L] b153-160 transition, compressed: the CELL climbs Gm - Cm - Ab
#     (Neapolitan; tp/timp silent) - D, D strokes, then D pedal pp with
#     va 8ths and the CELL' echo in ob1, fl1.
# [M] b161-168 S (the Mvt-II cantilena) in G MAJOR, vn1+fl1 p dolce, va
#     arpeggios, vc/cb pizz, hn12 pedal.
# [N] b169-176 S again, now sung by the CELLO (+cl1) in its tenor
#     register (the Mvt-II slow-movement colour), vn1 runs the CELL in G
#     MAJOR (CELLM) above it, cb pizz + fg bass, va soft sustained notes.
# [O] b177-184 broadening cadence in G major, cresc. to f.
# [P] b185-200 closing group in G MAJOR (as b81-96 a minor 3rd lower):
#     CELLM in strings in octaves vs syncopated winds; winds take the
#     CELL on Em - Am - D - D7; accented cadence C - G/B - Am - D - G;
#     hammer-strokes, b200 one G-major stroke + silence.

